 *
 * Issue #2327 Stage B (BUILD-ONLY): crops the ISP's INPUT frame (IMX335's
 * native 1296x972 2x2-binned SRGGB10P output) down to 1280x960 -- the same
 * output size IMX296's own ROI crop already produces, so this example's
 * buffer pool (overlay-imx335.conf) matches overlay-imx296.conf's sizing
 * exactly instead of needing a third pool size.
 *
 * crop-x0/crop-y0 (zephyr/dts/bindings/video/vsi,isp-pico.yaml) feed
 * isp_pico.c's out_form_rect: width = port_fmt.width - (left << 1), height =
 * port_fmt.height - (top << 1) -- i.e. both properties crop SYMMETRICALLY
 * (left AND right by crop-x0, top AND bottom by crop-y0), not from one
 * corner. 1296 - 1280 = 16, so crop-x0 = 8 (8 px off each side); 972 - 960 =
 * 12, so crop-y0 = 6 (6 px off top and bottom).
 */
&isp {
	crop-x0 = <8>;
	crop-y0 = <6>;
};
